(what it doesn't do yet) This shows the image mechanism works, not that the compiler runs in it. codex-19 says so itself at line 2836:
- the translated modules are *registered*, but their initialisers haven't run;
- no declaration probe has been executed;
- `lean_py.marshal`, which turns native Lean objects into Python values, is still blocked on metaclass behaviour.

previous_reply_acts.text:
(where the analogy holds) In a proof assistant, search can be fast and unsound because the kernel re-checks every candidate it returns. Here the warm image can skip cold starts, keep stale caches and let us redefine functions mid-run. The Python probe then checks the result:
- from an empty cache;
- with the byte checks;
- with a test that fails before the fix;
- with a Lean citation.
